A||||4||SibERThuG||Car is dead... Can You Help Me???||||8||
Z||000000||SibERThuG||11-01-2000||12:11 AM||||All day today, my car has slightly "buckled" or "bucked" in the rear under high(er) RPM's (when accelerating). I thought it was the clutch slipping, but at about 10:00 tonight it became more violent. As I came down a road my engine was extremly quiet and seemed like it was not running, even though it was. The RPM's were low even as I accelerated hard. It seemed as no fuel was being pushed into the engine. As I started to pull off the road my car backfired, and as I let off the acceleration and stopped, it died. Now it starts to turn over, but won't. Is my fuel pump broken?? What happened? Is this an expensive fix?? HELP ME!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Robbie<BR>88' Formula||||reg||8
Z||000001||Phil||11-01-2000||07:04 AM||||Check coil and/or ign. module||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||11-01-2000||08:19 AM||||...and the plug wires.  Run it at night (in the dark) and look for arcking.  No-cost diagnosis.  Plug wires are (typically) cheaper than ign. coil, and less trouble than pickup coil, so I'd try plug wires first.  But that's just me...  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||robertjay||11-01-2000||08:26 AM||||My V6 did a similar thing to me (except for the dieing part), and it was my catalytic convertor was clogged.  The material inside of it had come apart and lodged itself in the tail pipe.  It felt like a fuel delivery problem, it wouldn't rev over 2000 rpm's while driving, and only about 3500 in neutral, and it was pretty quiet.  So after changing a few parts, like fuel filter, cap and rotor, checking and adjusting the timing, one good bang on the cat and it got a little better.  Hope this helps, good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000004||SibERThuG||11-01-2000||12:22 PM||||Thanks guys... I've got a mechanic doing it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> and I will pass the info along.<P>------------------<BR>Robbie<BR>88' Formula||||reg||1
